  // Action implementation
}
```

The `Attributes` interface allows specifying additional attributes and events that an action enables on the applied element. This is primarily for TypeScript typings and does not affect runtime behavior. An example interface might include:
```typescript
interface Attributes {
  newprop?: string;
  'on:event': (event: <boolean>) => void;
}
```

