Use the :global() modifier inside a <style> block:
```svelte
<style>
:global(body) {
  margin: 0;
}
</style>
```
This applies the style globally to the <body> element across the entire application.

Use the :global {} block inside a <style> tag:
```svelte
<style>
:global {
  div { ... }
  p { ... }
}
</style>
```
This applies styles globally to all <div> and <p> elements in the application.

Use the nested :global() modifier:
```svelte
div :global(strong) {
  color: goldenrod;
}
```
This applies the goldenrod color to all <strong> elements inside <div> elements, regardless of the component.

Prepend the keyframe name with -global- in the @keyframes declaration:
```svelte
<style>
@keyframes -global-my-animation-name {
  /* code goes here */
}
</style>
```
The -global- prefix ensures the keyframe is accessible across the entire application.

Use the :global() modifier with class selectors:
```svelte
p:global(.big.red) {
  /* styles for <p> elements with class="big red" */
}
```
This applies styles to elements with multiple classes, even if applied programmatically.

```svelte
.a :global {
  .b .c .d { ... }
}
```
This applies styles to .b .c .d elements inside an .a element, across any component.

